{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":1220,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"Dynamic programming counts binary words of length 14 avoiding 000 and 111.\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"111\" and \"000\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 identical bits. This is classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run of length 2. For each bit, but we can combine symmetrical. Let's define:\n\nLet A_n = number of sequences length n ending with a single bit (i.e., last run length 1). Let B_n = number ending with run length 2. Then total T_n = A_n + B_n.\n\nTransitions: To get A_{n+1}, we need last bit different from previous bit, so previous run length can be 1 or 2. So A_{n+1} = T_n.\n\nTo get B_{n+1}, we need last two bits same, so previous run length must be 1 and same bit. So B_{n+1} = A_n.\n\nInitial: For n=1: sequences of length1: \"0\",\"1\". Each has run length1. So A_1=2, B_1=0.\n\nCompute up to n=14.\n\nLet's iterate.\n\nn=1: A=2,B=0,T=2\nn=2: A2 = T1=2, B2 = A1=2 => T2=4\nn=3: A3 = T2=4, B3 = A2=2 => T3=6\nn=4: A4 = T3=6, B4 = A3=4 => T4=10\nn=5: A5 = T4=10, B5 = A4=6 => T5=16\nn=6: A6 = T5=16, B6 = A5=10 => T6=26\nn=7: A7 = T6=26, B7 = A6=16 => T7=42\nn=8: A8 = T7=42, B8 = A7=26 => T8=68\nn=9: A9 = T8=68, B9 = A8=42 => T9=110\nn=10: A10 = T9=110, B10 = A9=68 => T10=178\nn=11: A11 = T10=178, B11 = A10=110 => T11=288\nn=12: A12 = T11=288, B12 = A11=178 => T12=466\nn=13: A13 = T12=466, B13 = A12=288 => T13=754\nn=14: A14 = T13=754, B14 = A13=466 => T14=1220\n\nThus answer 1220. Provide final JSON."}}],"created":1790944599,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.ggu